ous and so  so carefully put together that it's just  so enjoyable to watch  so if you ever have a spare 20 minutes i  think most of his videos are  to just sit down and watch him put this  masterpiece together it is genuinely an  enjoyable experience just to watch his  content and last but not least channel  number five  is called the local project and it is  more specific i guess to australians and  australian architecture  it takes a lot of the architecture  around australia as well as new zealand  actually in more recent times and  showcases it and takes it through the  journey  so they'll take the architect who  actually designed it on board  and get them to explain the project  whilst involving the clients and  explaining that emotive story you not  only get to see the beautiful  architecture that's  designed and built around australia you  also get to see the truly humbling  stories and the process behind it the  decisions behind  every single decision if you're in  architecture you know that you don't go  just and choose one tile for the sake of  it  looks pretty you go there to actually  make a statement  and with all these houses and all these  projects they're multi-million dollar  projects  they're the best of the best most the  time they're concrete which is a bit odd  but i genuinely do love concrete houses  lately so  it's a good thing hence probably why  i've selected it but yeah it's  just incredible to see the thought  process of other professionals  in the same space without the judgment  of going  uh i'm going to go over there and talk  to this professional and they're just  going to give me a whole bunch of  mumbo-jumbo that i don't understand and  they probably won't even tell me what  they actually did or why they did it or  how they did it because it's a trade  secret  so i think the local project that was a  bit of a ramble sorry  the local project does some phenomenal  stuff  and they truly do deserve some love so  make sure you go down to 